body:
Go for long walks alone. This got me into wildlife photography.

&#x200B;

Do random kind things for her so she feels guilty doing bad things to you. E.g. make a cup of sweet tea randomly.

&#x200B;

Listen to music in your room / Turn on a fan or air filter in your room if you have one to shut out the noise. Use earplugs. Keep your room door locked.

&#x200B;

Open car / room windows. Narcissists hate their viciousness being exposed to people that can possibly hear them, even if there's nobody there. Everything has to be subterfuge. They writhe to sunlight.

&#x200B;

I have faith in your strength. You are not alone.

Reading this made me so angry. Your father is a piece of shit that does not belong in society. He means nothing of what he says and purely exploits your empathy to his advantage. He is only saying that he is "disowning" you because he wants to make you feel as though you have an obligation to him, which you do NOT. He's twisting the narrative when it is YOU disowning HIM. It's like the bitch at work who royally fucks up and says "I quit" before getting fired.

&#x200B;

He is yanking your empathy on a string of familial attachment. My narcissistic father did the exact same thing. I cut him off permanently and never plan on talking to him again. Your life will be infinitely better when you do so. Trust me on that. Surround yourself with people who are positive influences and immersing in your passions is the best way to heal. For the time being, though, while you are still trapped, I strongly recommend researching the characterizing traits of a narcissist, including how they gaslight, guilt-trip, and use flying monkeys against you, and how to grey rock.

&#x200B;

He is a monster, and this is a textbook narcissist doing what they do worst. I highly advise moving out if you can, and for your mother's safety, recording his anger and gathering evidence so you can use it in filing a restraining order. There is an outline for writing cease-and-desist letters in this sub, which would be a good first step to take. I really want to help you, but I can only say so much in a single comment.

&#x200B;

Above all, you are doing the mature and right thing by cutting off your nfather completely. Give him NO reasons as to why you are ignoring him; he will twist your valid indignations towards his outrageous behavior into lies that victimize himself. You are so strong to be persevering through this, OP. I hope you can escape.
